     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum metformin dose. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, usually given as 850 mg three times daily. The extended-release maximum is 2,000 mg/day. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Some possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day total.** This could be 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO** at a different frequency.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it. If you really do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that. Include a note with the rationale so pharmacy and nursing can see it."
      }
     ],
